    "client_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-c10000000001",
    "notes": [
      "notices is a pull-only table keyed by one bigint column, id (D-row-key): the server numbers its rows and devices only read them, so the transcript carries no local write and no push.",
      "a pk is the key text, so a bigint key travels as its plain decimal string: '7', '10', '9'. The rows also carry id itself, as the table renders it.",
      "the stream is ordered by seq, never by pk: '10' sorts before '7' byte for byte, and the page still delivers 7, 10, 9 in the order the server wrote them (P:keyset-pagination-and-delivery-bound).",
      "the step-4 page delivers live rows of owner user-a, which grants that bucket value, so the step-8 page carries the tombstone of notice 9 under its decimal pk (D-tombstone-delivery)."
    ],
